MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Very Best of Peter, Paul and Mary feels like a natural next choice because Simon & Garfunkel and Melanie have me interested in familiar folk songs and vocal harmonies, especially in a best-of collection.",
    "The Smile Sessions connects with the adventurous sixties pop I enjoyed in Sgt. Pepper, while 4 Way Street connects with the folk-rock side of my Jonathan Edwards and classic-rock listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Tab Benoit's blues and Glenn Miller's big-band music do not match the folk and sixties pop I want now; enjoying some standards does not make every older musical style equally appealing.",
    "A later Chicago album is less appealing today than familiar classic-era material, and titles such as The Singer, Enchanted, Older, and A Christmas Album leave me unsure which artist or recording I would be choosing."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in older recordings seems to have been stretched into an interest in older music generally, even when the sound differs substantially from my folk and classic-rock choices.",
    "My recent Christmas selection seems to have been taken as enough reason to suggest another holiday album, although the artist and songs matter more to me than the seasonal connection alone."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated choices of best-of albums and compilations suggest that recognizable songs are a strong draw right now, which makes a later studio album a less natural next choice.",
    "The connections among Simon & Garfunkel, Melanie, and Jonathan Edwards matter more to my current choices than my occasional interest in standards or pop; I need a clear musical connection before choosing something less familiar."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in folk and sixties pop but extended it too broadly to other older recordings and holiday music."
}
